>> title: Frozen Spring Rolls with Dipping Sauce, Air Fryer
>> category: Dumplings & Rolls
>> tags: frozen, spring rolls, air fryer, basket, snack, dipping sauce
>> counters: The Air Fryer & the Pot
>> aka: air fryer spring rolls, frozen spring rolls, frozen egg rolls, nuoc cham dipping sauce, spring rolls without a fryer
>> servings: 4
>> time: 20 min
>> slack: narrow — a roll left past its colour splits at the seam and the filling comes out into the basket, which is the one thing that turns this into washing-up
>> washing-up: the basket, the bowl
>> keeps: not at all — the wrapper softens as it cools and goes chewy; cook the number you are going to eat

>> step: Straight from the freezer into a preheated 5.7 L basket, one layer. A 3.5 L basket is two batches, not more minutes.
Frozen, not thawed. Thawed wrappers go limp and stick to the basket.

>> step: stir the dipping sauce in the bowl it is served in
Stir @fish sauce{2%Tbs}, @rice vinegar{2%Tbs}, @sugar{1%Tbs}, @warm water{3%Tbs}, @garlic{1%clove}(grated), @red chile{1}(sliced thin) together in a #bowl{}.

>> step: roast in the basket 190°C (375°F), 10–12 min, one layer
Roast @frozen spring rolls{12}(straight from the freezer) in a preheated #air fryer basket{} at 190°C (375°F) for ~air fry{11%min}, one layer and not touching.

>> step: turn at halfway — blistered and biscuit brown, seams still closed
Turn @&(~1)spring rolls{} once.

>> step: scatter the cilantro, sauce alongside
Scatter @cilantro{2%Tbs}(picked) over @&(~1)spring rolls{} and serve @&(~3)dipping sauce{} alongside.

>> step: A wet batter would blow off in this draught. A frozen wrapper is already dry, which is why this one works.
Dry wrappers hold. Wet batter lifts off before it sets.
